# Cursor Rules -- Signalboard (Firebase App)

Read CLAUDE.md before starting any task. It contains project architecture,
commands, and conventions that must be followed.

## Project Structure

This is an npm workspaces monorepo:
- `apps/web` -- Next.js 14 App Router (customer dashboard)
- `apps/functions` -- Cloud Functions v2 (event-driven + HTTP callable)
- `apps/bot` -- Discord.js bot
- `databases/` -- Firestore security rules and indexes
- `packages/ui` -- Shared design system components (`@sig/ui`)
- `types/` -- Shared TypeScript types (`@sig/types`)

## General Rules

- Use TypeScript strict mode. No `any` types without a justifying comment.
- Use named exports everywhere. Default exports only for Next.js pages/layouts.
- Import shared types as `@sig/types` and UI components as `@sig/ui`.
- Colocate test files next to source: `handler.ts` -> `handler.test.ts`.
- Keep files under 250 lines. Extract into smaller modules when approaching the limit.
- All Firestore writes happen through Cloud Functions, never directly from the web client.

## TypeScript Conventions

- Prefer `interface` for object shapes. Use `type` for unions and utility types.
- Firestore document types defined in `types/firestore/` with `WithId<T>` wrapper for client-side use.
- Use `as const` objects instead of enums. Derive union types from values.
- Function parameters: destructured objects for 3+ parameters.
- Use `satisfies` operator for type-safe literal objects.

## Firestore Patterns

- Use typed converters for all Firestore references:

```typescript
import { converter } from "@/lib/firestore/converter";
import type { Signal } from "@sig/types";

const signalRef = doc(db, `orgs/${orgId}/signals/${signalId}`).withConverter(
  converter<Signal>()
);
```

- Collection references centralized in `apps/web/src/lib/firestore/collections.ts`.
- All documents must include `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `createdBy` fields.
- Use `serverTimestamp()` for timestamp fields, never `new Date()`.
- Batch writes for multi-document updates. Use transactions when reads are needed.
- Subcollection paths: `orgs/{orgId}/[collection]/{docId}`.

## Cloud Functions (apps/functions)

- One function per file in `src/handlers/`.
- Name functions descriptively: `onSignalCreated`, `onMemberInvited`, `handleWebhook`.
- Use v2 function declarations:

```typescript
import { onDocumentCreated } from "firebase-functions/v2/firestore";

export const onSignalCreated = onDocumentCreated(
  "orgs/{orgId}/signals/{signalId}",
  async (event) => {
    const signal = event.data?.data();
    // ...
  }
);
```

- HTTP callable functions validate input with Zod schemas.
- Set appropriate memory, timeout, and concurrency in function options.
- Idempotency: event-triggered functions must handle duplicate invocations.

## React / Next.js (apps/web)

- Server components by default. Add `"use client"` only when necessary.
- Use App Router patterns: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`.
- Data fetching in server components using Firebase Admin SDK (server-side) or Firestore hooks (client-side).
- Auth state managed via `AuthProvider` context wrapping the app.
- Protected routes use `middleware.ts` to check Firebase Auth session cookie.

## Design System (@sig/ui)

- All UI primitives come from `@sig/ui`. Do not add competing UI libraries.
- Component variants defined with `cva` (class-variance-authority).
- Import components: `import { Button, Card, Badge } from "@sig/ui"`.
- Colors use semantic tokens: `primary`, `secondary`, `accent`, `destructive`, `muted`.
- Follow the existing component API patterns. Check `packages/ui/src/` for examples.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS exclusively. No CSS modules, styled-components, or inline styles.
- Use `cn()` for conditional class merging (clsx + tailwind-merge).
- Mobile-first responsive: base -> `sm:` -> `md:` -> `lg:`.
- Dark mode supported via `dark:` variant. Always provide dark mode styles.

## Discord Bot (apps/bot)

- Command handlers in `src/commands/`. One file per command.
- Use Discord.js slash command builders for registration.
- Embed builders for rich responses. Keep embeds concise.
- Rate limit awareness: respect Discord API limits.
- Access Firestore through Firebase Admin SDK initialized in `src/lib/firebase.ts`.

## Testing

- Unit tests: Vitest with mocked dependencies.
- Firestore rules tests: `@firebase/rules-unit-testing` against emulator.
- Integration tests: run against Firebase Emulator Suite.
- Test naming: `describe("SignalService")` / `it("creates a signal with valid data")`.
- Factories in `tests/factories/` for generating test documents.

## Git Workflow

- Branch from `dev`. Never commit to `main` or `dev` directly.
- Branch naming: `feat/SIG-123-short-description` or `fix/SIG-456-short-description`.
- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `docs:`.
- PR titles: `type(scope): description (SIG-123)`.
- Keep PRs focused. One logical change per PR.

## Security

- Org-scoping enforced everywhere: users see only their org's data.
- Custom claims (`orgId`, `role`) set via Cloud Functions, never from client.
- Firestore rules validate org-scoping on every read and write.
- API keys and secrets stored in Secret Manager, accessed via `defineSecret()`.
- Never commit `.env` files. Use `.env.example` with placeholder values.

## Error Handling

- Cloud Functions: `HttpsError` with codes (`not-found`, `permission-denied`, `invalid-argument`).
- Web app: error boundaries per route segment with user-friendly messages.
- Structured logging: `functions.logger.info()` with context fields.
- Bot: catch errors, log context, send user-facing embed with "something went wrong" message.

## Deterministic agent workflow

Same phases every session: **classify** (bug/feature/refactor/chore/docs/investigation) → **context** (read CLAUDE.md + similar code) → **plan** (if 3+ files or cross-workspace) → **implement** → **validate** (npm run typecheck, lint, test locally before push) → **review** (diff + test mapping) → **ship** (branch, commit, PR). Use a **dedicated branch** per task; use **separate git worktrees** for parallel agent runs. **Implement until green**; **review until done** on the same branch.
